+## Deploy on Wasmer
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=barryclark%2Fjekyll-now)
+
+Wasmer detects this as a Jekyll site: it runs `bundle init && bundle add jekyll -v 4.3.0` (there is no `Gemfile`), then `jekyll build`, and serves the `_site` folder. The button opens Wasmer's import page for this public repository, where you review the configuration and click Deploy; it does not create a copy of the repository in your GitHub account; to deploy your own blog, fork Jekyll Now, edit `_config.yml` and your posts, then import your fork on Wasmer. Because only Jekyll is installed, the `jekyll-sitemap` and `jekyll-feed` plugins listed in `_config.yml` are not run there.
+
 ## Moar!
 
 I've created a more detailed walkthrough, [**Build A Blog With Jekyll And GitHub Pages**](http://www.smashingmagazine.com/2014/08/01/build-blog-jekyll-github-pages/) over at the Smashing Magazine website. Check it out if you'd like a more detailed walkthrough and some background on Jekyll. :metal:
